{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:32:02-07:00","id":100343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100304#post100304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking on a Gentry, in a fight, inside one of their own domains within Faerie?<br /> <br /> <br /> No. Vampire Methusalah couldn't. Archmages would fall. Luna would likely be unable to do so either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not be nonsensical. Luna's scale warrants more in the vein of <i>war on Faerie.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T16:43:52-07:00","id":100462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100343#post100343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not be nonsensical. Luna's scale warrants more in the vein of <i>war on Faerie.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> And Archmage scale doesn't? Methuselah wouldn't play a terribly complex chess-master game?<br /> I rattled them off because they're all god level beings. Gentry could likely take any of them within their own domain. Put same Gentry into the Hisil or Astral? Or whatever shadowy Lower Depth realm the strix call home? The respective god-level being will hold the advantage.<br /> <br /> <br /> An Exile, or whatever the demon equivalent to an archmage/methuselah/true fae/spirit god is, would likely stand a chance against the Gentry if he/she had Infrastructure to back her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-27-2014, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:10:07-07:00","id":100472,"title":"","content":"Given that Gentry pretty much -are- their Domain, yeah... in most cases all you're fucking around with is an individual Title/manifestation anyhow without ever directly confronting the thing (well, if you use Equinox Road).<br /> <br /> Even running by by Imperial Mysteries guideline ideas for god-tier things (which I can take or leave), Gentry usually are higher than your &quot;average&quot; Archmage, and they don't really play by &quot;the rules&quot; very well regardless. &quot;Oh, you conquered faerie? That's a nice story. But in my story that didn't happen. Have fun with your own reality shard, we've got more interesting things to do after that conflict gets boring&quot;. Linear event progression and time. Meh.<br /> <br /> Even then, they were what, Rank 7-ish as discrete entities? Luna herself was presented as Rank 8 if memory serves (and even then, the broad rankings really don't account for what they can respectively do individually outside of the broadest tacked on assumptions. Someone who's got handy access right now can correct me there. Honestly, once you're on that 6+ scale it's pretty irrelevant anyhow beyond theoretical &quot;maybes&quot;. It's so damn up in the air as to not matter. Anything could happen.<br /> <br /> And for the record, I'd see Luna as a little bitch in Arcadia anyhow regardless of her Rank. She's one spirit, massive in scope and scale and allies, but -still- dealing with a literal host of exceedingly powerful gods that don't play by her rules. War on faerie? Not bloody likely anymore than the Oracles or others truly conquered it in a meaningful way. Much the same in reverse with the Gentry going after The Shadow; it's effectively war on an entire divergent reality, not just the individuals present.<br /> <br /> You don't waltz into the mouth of hell, then complain about it not conforming to your expectations.<br /> <br /> As is, we don't really know what the full cap/heights of vampires even are. You get odd allusions to the Tremere, Archmages of Vampirism as potentials by some writers and other tidbits here and there in other gamelines, nevermind who the hell knows what The Blood itself is really all about; odds are there are god-tier vampires out there just as much a threat (and honestly, once you're dealing with that level you're not really using the base mechanics on any splats end anyhow).<br /> <br /> Odds are likely that you won't ever see them definied to any extent because it's not really relevant to anything in V:tR except fanboy pet splat battles and occasionally putting some context down for Mage when it's going into Tier-4-esque craziness. Gods of the Blood? The Great Darkness the Strix come from? Something else entirely? Who knows. But what Vampire game are you going to be playing where that's ever really going to be important enough? Once you're playing that scope, the game becomes something -drastically- different. Odds are the vampiric entity does too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 03-27-2014, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:22:44-07:00","id":100478,"title":"","content":"when i read on how demons get in Arcadia they cant get out without the help of a changeling or denizen of the hedge apparently demon got the exploit called rip the gates where they can enter any world that on world of darkness and for arcadia if they were to enter they can only get out when a person has the power to open the doors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 03-27-2014, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:27:24-07:00","id":100479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100472#post100472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for the record, I'd see Luna as a little bitch in Arcadia anyhow regardless of her Rank. She's one spirit, massive in scope and scale and allies, but -still- dealing with a literal host of exceedingly powerful gods that don't play by her rules. War on faerie? Not bloody likely anymore than the Oracles or others truly conquered it in a meaningful way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was speaking in terms of the fact that there are Rank 7 Lunes <i>on the books</i> that by definition answer to Luna and a single Fae does not equate to a/the Queen of the Shadow any more than it does the G-M or the Horsemen.<br /> <br /> Luna is more likely to engage with the Fae as a group because getting to her Rank is impossible without changing the fundamental nature of the universe. UnAscended archmagi and greater Incarnae, subsouls and Royal Avatars aside, can more or less still be interacted with as individuals, however powerful. The Fae don't have enough of a stable position in the world that they can be placed above that point without getting into speculation on Wyrd Transcendence. You don't compare Fae to the God-Machine, you compare them to archangels; ditto comparisons to Luna and the Lunes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:34:30-07:00","id":100485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100478#post100478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when i read on how demons get in Arcadia they cant get out without the help of a changeling or denizen of the hedge apparently demon got the exploit called rip the gates where they can enter any world that on world of darkness and for arcadia if they were to enter they can only get out when a person has the power to open the doors.</div> </div> </div> </div> Rip the Doors is... problematic. I mean, yeah, you can appear in the Hisil, Underworld, Hedge (note! the Hedge is very much not the same as Faerie/Arcadia), or Astral. But it doesn't promise an easy exit back out of any of those realms. As well, there's still potentially Gears there. <br /> <br /> Or, even worse, no God Machine, and you're completely cut off from any supply of aether. At which point, you're in a hostile land with a very limited amount of ammo. And no promise of safe escape. Nothing stops Embeds, Exploits, Gadgets or Demon Forms from working in those four realms (though, in Faerie/Arcadia properly, all bets are off). But you don't have a lot of juice, and you're in hostile territory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:34:37-07:00","id":100486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100479#post100479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was speaking in terms of the fact that there are Rank 7 Lunes <i>on the books</i> that by definition answer to Luna and a single Fae does not equate to a/the Queen of the Shadow any more than it does the G-M or the Horsemen.<br /> <br /> Luna is more likely to engage with the Fae as a group because getting to her Rank is impossible without changing the fundamental nature of the universe. UnAscended archmagi and greater Incarnae, subsouls and Royal Avatars aside, can more or less still be interacted with as individuals, however powerful. The Fae don't have enough of a stable position in the world that they can be placed above that point without getting into speculation on Wyrd Transcendence. You don't compare Fae to the God-Machine, you compare them to archangels; ditto comparisons to Luna and the Lunes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing that I could think that can actually fight Luna is the god machine himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:47:00-07:00","id":100494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100343#post100343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not be nonsensical. Luna's scale warrants more in the vein of <i>war on Faerie.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, the Gentry operate in an entirely different way to Luna, along with any of the other Gods. Luna has a defined set of powers, enormous yes, but she has her limits and they are defined by... lets call them the laws of physics for simplicity.<br /> <br /> The True Fae on the other hand only have the powers and limitations that they agree to. If they refuse to agree that Luna can hurt them (and they haven't already made pacts Luna can use), then She can't hurt them, simple as that. Of course, fair is fair. If Luna (/ Luna's reflection in the Wyrd) doesn't agree to be hurt then the Gentry can't touch her.<br /> <br /> <br /> A fight between Luna and a True Fae would go one of three ways:<br /> <br /> 1) The True Fae has already made agreements that Luna can exploit, it's probably dead.<br /> 2) The True Fae and Luna start by agreeing a set of rules, this would probably give the True Fae a modest advantage because the Gentry has a homefield advantage at negotiations; it wants an interesting story so it can't be too powerful but it also to win (think of the difference between a 0-35 exp Changeling and the Arcadian Huntsman in the corebook)<br /> 3) The True Fae and Luna can't agree on rules, and no fight happens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Finally. Imperial Mysteries is a Mage book. Neither Luna or the True Fae are form Mage, so it's not really relevant to this discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:48:53-07:00","id":100496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100486#post100486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that I could think that can actually fight Luna is the god machine himself.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sol, the spirit of the Sun. Gaia, the spirit of the Earth, who's actually rank 10 and could crush Luna with little effort. Gentry in their corner of Faerie could do it. Gnosis 10, Spirit 9 archmage stands a hell of a chance.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing about the &quot;patrons&quot; of the various supernaturals. At a certain point, they're all roughly equal in power. And that's way outside the league of the average demon, even if they used the Going Loud option.<br /> <br /> I think, however, that you're just using the name &quot;Arcadia&quot; wrong. No one actually goes to Arcadia, also known as Faerie. The Hedge itself is not Arcadia/Faerie. Inside of Faerie, the Gentry are absolute. They rewrite all laws of reality to suit their whims - even all the backdoors that Demons rely on for their powers. Now, inside the Hedge is a different matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T18:03:03-07:00","id":100498,"title":"","content":"The spirit of the sun is Helios, Luna's brother - who's the same Rank as her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T18:08:17-07:00","id":100501,"title":"","content":"Does Rip the Gates specify that you end up in a safe place in said other world? Cause a lot of the Hedge is made up of the Thorns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T18:08:50-07:00","id":100502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100496#post100496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sol, the spirit of the Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Helios.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaia, the spirit of the Earth, who's actually rank 10 and could crush Luna with little effort. </div> </div> </div>Rank 9 and of questionable reality. Rank 10 being &quot;beyond manifest conception&quot; is not a descriptor that is just for show.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Inside of Faerie, the Gentry are absolute. They rewrite all laws of reality to suit their whims - even all the backdoors that Demons rely on for their powers. </div> </div> </div>Faerie's laws of hospitality mean that if you've made it inside, you're there as <i>somebody's</i> guest, and there are obviously hard limits on the laws of reality that they can't change - the ban on cold iron, for instance, or the need to challenge other Fae to claim their Titles.<br /> <br /> Also, the Fae steal a lot of stuff - it wouldn't be terribly surprising, in a crossover with the Unchained, if one of the Strangers happened to &quot;borrow&quot; some of the Machine's shortcuts to preserve fair play with its &quot;guests.&quot; The Wyrd does rather demand that they play in something resembling a fair manner - who knows how, say, Reality Enforcement might interact with such a space?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T18:23:29-07:00","id":100508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100501#post100501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Rip the Gates specify that you end up in a safe place in said other world? Cause a lot of the Hedge is made up of the Thorns.</div> </div> </div> </div>its based on success if its normal then yes you could be in a dangerous place or even in a true fae home. But if its exceptional then they wont be bothered for the next hour or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T18:25:38-07:00","id":100509,"title":"","content":"There isn't much that can deal with the Gentry in Arcadia assuming they don't want to be dealt with. A normal demon has little chance outside of hoping that they think the demon winning would make for a good story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T18:35:31-07:00","id":100516,"title":"","content":"Luna likely has a connection to Arcadia, its also Called the Lunargent Thorn after all, she definitely has some connection to its madness. For all we know Luna could be one of the Ruling forces of Arcadia, an aspect of its Wyrd.<br /> <br /> We don't really have full rules on the Celestines, people guess at their power and even Existence. They are major beings and likely have reflections throughout the Tellurian. The Concept of the Moon Exists in Arcadia definitely. The Very Season and Stone itself exist their as major beings, and not as Fae. The Gentry are not the only beings in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> We just don't know the Connection the Spirit of the Moon has with Platonic Ideal of the Moon, but it would be foolish to think their was absolutely no connection.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100485#post100485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rip the Doors is... problematic. I mean, yeah, you can appear in the Hisil, Underworld, Hedge (note! the Hedge is very much not the same as Faerie/Arcadia), or Astral. But it doesn't promise an easy exit back out of any of those realms. As well, there's still potentially Gears there.<br /> <br /> Or, even worse, no God Machine, and you're completely cut off from any supply of aether. At which point, you're in a hostile land with a very limited amount of ammo. And no promise of safe escape. Nothing stops Embeds, Exploits, Gadgets or Demon Forms from working in those four realms (though, in Faerie/Arcadia properly, all bets are off). But you don't have a lot of juice, and you're in hostile territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you produce Aether just by being in Demon Form, so not an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T02:37:38-07:00","id":100654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100502#post100502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faerie's laws of hospitality mean that if you've made it inside, you're there as <i>somebody's</i> guest</div> </div> </div> </div> Explicitly untrue as per Equinox Roads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100502#post100502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and there are obviously hard limits on the laws of reality that they can't change - the ban on cold iron</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually that might not be true. The ban on cold iron might be a weakness the fae agreed to - that is, they made a deal with a penalty clause of a weakness to iron and broke it. That's one of the options presented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100502#post100502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for instance, or the need to challenge other Fae to claim their Titles.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes.<br /> <br /> So the two limits you've uncovered are basically: Can't undo deals without the other guy agreeing. Can't remove the need for deals in the first place.<br /> <br /> Neither really have much cosmological implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T03:42:48-07:00","id":100668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100516#post100516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually you produce Aether just by being in Demon Form, so not an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, you're a receptor for aether, not a generator. The game points out that many demons hang out in places where the God Machine is because, if they isolate themselves, there's a good chance they'll run out of aether and be defenseless. Aether is a God Machine waste byproduct, not something they make on their own. If you travel to a realm (or, heck, even isolated stretch of forest) where the God Machine isn't present, there's a high chance you won't be able to gather energy even by assuming Demon Form.<br /> <br /> Even if you could, however, the book makes it pretty clear that you can be stuck in Demon Form without any aether. You only roll for more when you hit rock bottom... and you can fail that roll.<br /> <br /> So, I'm sorry, but it seems that the intent of the aether section that, if you separate yourself from the God Machine, there's a good chance you won't be able to gather aether. So I'm going to have to disagree with you on this point. Rules haven't been detailed, but then, most of the time crossover sections like that show up in supplement books, not the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T09:51:53-07:00","id":100766,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that Rip the Gates lets you enter: The Shadow, The Astral, The Hedge and the Underworld.<br /> <br /> I'm also pretty sure that it can get you out of any of these realms except the Hedge. Its in the sidebar next to the power in the Demon book.<br /> <br /> This is in keeping with the theme/metaphysics of the Hedge being sorta fixed in the methods by which one can leave it (namely through Hedge Gates or a Hallow Door, likely due to &quot;old agreements&quot; between the Hedge/Wyrd/Gentry and other realms.<br /> <br /> Personally, I find the Gentry get a little too much *love* by the fandom in these sorta discussions.<br /> <br /> (* By which I mean massive levels of fan-wank that broadly and loosely uses some ambiguities in the True Fae fluff to run with the idea that they are the most powerful thing in setting for the NWoD. Honestly, if your going with the idea that the Gentry are only weak to Cold Iron because they feel like being weak to it, rather then they were forced to break a deal with it once upon a time and that's still biting them in the ass (and proving...shock...horror...their fallible) then please acknowledge your bias towards them over other metaphysically similar groups.)<br /> <br /> Yeah we all love Changeling and its a great game and it was a sleeper hit for White Wolf back in the day and blah, blah, blah. Enough with the &quot;but the Gentry could...&quot; statements that pop up in the other forums all the damn time. <br /> <br /> People seem to forget that Arcadia is just one of many realms that seems attached to the world and that each has its own &quot;God&quot; equivelent and for narrative purposes they are all basically equal, basically. Yes the &quot;fine print&quot; of each is different and one might have a more obvious limitation in one area or have a more obvious weakness but they all ultimately fulfill the role of &quot;ancient slightly unknowable entity in the background that impacts on your life in way X&quot;. <br /> <br /> This is all, I might add, shockingly besides the point of this thread. Can a regular unchained take a Gentry in Arcadia? Short answer: No. <br /> <br /> If we are exploring the idea of can X god-archetype/equivalent take a Gentry in Arcadia the answer is:<br /> <br /> Yes for some, no for others and its all ultimately up to the what the ST decides is the case. <br /> <br /> For example I often put the Exarchs, God Machine or the Abyss at the top of the pecking order. My justification is that one of these redefined all of reality to suit them, one maintains reality as we understand it and one can and may inevitably destroy everything forever because it can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T10:05:43-07:00","id":100771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100766#post100766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(* By which I mean massive levels of fan-wank that broadly and loosely uses some ambiguities in the True Fae fluff to run with the idea that they are the most powerful thing in setting for the NWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Virtually every discussion on the matter that I've seen has indicated the opposite, because the Fae run up against the Predator Clause* and the Incarnae and Celestines don't.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* &quot;If it has stats, we can kill it!&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T10:09:28-07:00","id":100776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100771#post100771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Virtually every discussion on the matter that I've seen has indicated the opposite, because the Fae run up against the Predator Clause* and the Incarnae and Celestines don't.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* &quot;If it has stats, we can kill it!&quot;</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly I've had this point raised before. Pro-True Fae people always go to the argument of:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;One tiny aspect/actor/title has stats that you can interact with. The whole of a True Fae is beyond the ken of any muahahahahahah!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I may have added the evil laugh at the end for dramatic effect...but I hope the general argument is communicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T10:37:39-07:00","id":100789,"title":"","content":"IIRC, Mages who teleport in can't teleport back out, just like Demons. It has to do with the metaphysics of the Hedge. In the hedge, reality is loosely defined. Getting INTO the Hedge from Earth works because the earth, and its Gates, are the &quot;anchor&quot; for the user, giving a solid, stable concept that a Mage or Demon can rework/edit to allow entrance. Once inside the Hedge, reality becomes so fluid that hacking the code or rewriting the truth isn't so simple anymore. The Hedge is a place of chaos after all. Of course, getting into the Hedge is NOT the same as getting into Arcadia. It'd be as difficult for a Demon to get there as it would be for a changeling, except that demons would be considered outsiders to the natives. As for aether generation, I'd allow demonic form to get aether while on paths (the stability of the paths, connections to mortal gateways etc) but not while in the thorns (the chaos is almost reality-free, and any God influence is minimal and shredded). Inside of Arcadia, I'd say you can only receive aether if you make a pact with a gentry to be allowed aether (perhaps the Fae allows some aether into their realm, or they duplicate it) but this would have to be done in every individual domain. And above all, Gentry are tier 4 entities. Unless attacked on earth (where the GM/reality requires them to diminish), only a tier 4 being has Any clean shot taking one on. A primum 7 demon that hasn't become an archdemon MIGHT be able to take out an Actor, but itd be a small fraction of the whole Fae. Taking on a True Fae on their scale would probably require an Archdemon, and then things like Pax Arcana kick in. While Pax Arcana is theoretically just in a Mage system, it seems everyone abides from it (the Gentry claim to do so by their own wishes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T17:03:16-07:00","id":100967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100776#post100776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interestingly I've had this point raised before. Pro-True Fae people always go to the argument of:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;One tiny aspect/actor/title has stats that you can interact with. The whole of a True Fae is beyond the ken of any muahahahahahah!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I may have added the evil laugh at the end for dramatic effect...but I hope the general argument is communicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of that whole thing, to be honest, the only one that is potentially problematic are Realms. Props, Actors and Swarms all have stats (and as such can be killed, as outlined by Satchel :P ). By the very virtue of the fact that they have stats, it controls how many titles a Fae can have (because a Title gives Fae stats).<br /> <br /> And let's be honest here, if you're capable of bringing the axe down on an Actor or Swarm, you've got the capability to defeat a Fae's story for a Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T18:04:58-07:00","id":101012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100668#post100668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, you're a receptor for aether, not a generator. The game points out that many demons hang out in places where the God Machine is because, if they isolate themselves, there's a good chance they'll run out of aether and be defenseless. Aether is a God Machine waste byproduct, not something they make on their own. If you travel to a realm (or, heck, even isolated stretch of forest) where the God Machine isn't present, there's a high chance you won't be able to gather energy even by assuming Demon Form.<br /> <br /> Even if you could, however, the book makes it pretty clear that you can be stuck in Demon Form without any aether. You only roll for more when you hit rock bottom... and you can fail that roll.<br /> <br /> So, I'm sorry, but it seems that the intent of the aether section that, if you separate yourself from the God Machine, there's a good chance you won't be able to gather aether. So I'm going to have to disagree with you on this point. Rules haven't been detailed, but then, most of the time crossover sections like that show up in supplement books, not the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 110<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demonic Form: A demon\u2019s true form is a natural receptor<br /> for Aether. Whenever a demon assumes demonic form, she<br /> automatically generates a number of points of Aether equal to<br /> her Primum rating. If she runs out of Aether while in demonic<br /> form, her player may roll the demon\u2019s Primum, with each<br /> success restoring a point of Aether. </div> </div> </div>It does not say anywhere that you stop generating Aether based on location. The danger to this is simply its easier for the Godmachine to track you so most demons rely off of other methods to accumulate Aether, but since you are far away from the God Machines Forces this is a suitable method of accessing Aether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T20:05:50-07:00","id":101045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=101012#post101012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does not say anywhere that you stop generating Aether based on location. The danger to this is simply its easier for the Godmachine to track you so most demons rely off of other methods to accumulate Aether, but since you are far away from the God Machines Forces this is a suitable method of accessing Aether.</div> </div> </div> </div> Read a bit earlier where it talks about how demons eschew going anywhere away from the God Machine, since they're afraid of running out of aether. Thematically, it seems to be part of the game. Just because we haven't been given hard rules (yet!), doesn't mean its not a concern we should focus on. <br /> <br /> And, as I said, the core book isn't the place for that, since it assumes you ARE facing the god machine and not running off into the middle of the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T21:21:42-07:00","id":101061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=101045#post101045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Read a bit earlier where it talks about how demons eschew going anywhere away from the God Machine, since they're afraid of running out of aether. Thematically, it seems to be part of the game. Just because we haven't been given hard rules (yet!), doesn't mean its not a concern we should focus on.<br /> <br /> And, as I said, the core book isn't the place for that, since it assumes you ARE facing the god machine and not running off into the middle of the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I can see Inquisitors going to the hedge for knowledge tempter their for pacts with gentry's. Psycho chomps for whatever resource they want and for most demons a place to hide I don't think the god machine has a lot of angels in the hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T21:40:02-07:00","id":101068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=101045#post101045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Read a bit earlier where it talks about how demons eschew going anywhere away from the God Machine, since they're afraid of running out of aether. Thematically, it seems to be part of the game. Just because we haven't been given hard rules (yet!), doesn't mean its not a concern we should focus on.<br /> <br /> And, as I said, the core book isn't the place for that, since it assumes you ARE facing the god machine and not running off into the middle of the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read my post at all? Your Demon form isn't supposed to be the method you use to regain Aether, its a small concession prize because it means you are already opening up to the God Machines Radar and that is dangerous virtually everywhere. But going someplace far removed from the Godmachine opens up the option, its one of the main principles of why Demons are trying to make Hell. You have produced no reason at all for why it should not work from what we know in the core rules, you are only guessing that it work because for some reason its an exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T01:37:11-07:00","id":101135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100766#post100766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(* By which I mean massive levels of fan-wank that broadly and loosely uses some ambiguities in the True Fae fluff to run with the idea that they are the most powerful thing in setting for the NWoD. Honestly, if your going with the idea that the Gentry are only weak to Cold Iron because they feel like being weak to it, rather then they were forced to break a deal with it once upon a time and that's still biting them in the ass (and proving...shock...horror...their fallible) then please acknowledge your bias towards them over other metaphysically similar groups.)</div> </div> </div> </div> While both ideas could easily be true. Though I don't recall anyone here denying the idea that they broke a deal with Iron.<br /> <br /> The simple fact, though, is that the Gentry are <u><b>both</b></u>the strongest and the weakest of the gods. Their powers are bounded only by what they can get reality to agree they can do. In other words they are theoretically limitless, while someone like Luna has limits - She is weaker than Gaia for example. <br /> <br /> At the same time the True Fae can't do anything to anyone unless they have an agreement in place. If any of the Firstborn or an Archmage decided to try and exterminate humanity, we're in big trouble. If the Gentry all united to destroy humanity, we could stop them by just refusing to talk to their diplomats. (Presumably whatever contract lets them abduct does not extend to genocide)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T01:47:57-07:00","id":101142,"title":"","content":"The Gentry don't have to make new contracts any time they do anything. They made several wide contracts since the Dawn of Time, like with Death for example. The fact that you are even interacting with one of the Others indicates they are already vulnerable because they are interacting with you.<br /> <br /> The Fae that don't have suitable contracts are likely beyond your reach in some far off axis of Arcadia. Its like the Shinma of Exalted, the Fae that we are seeing on Earth are the ones that have a relationship with the basic Shinma of the Universe, in the NWOD's case meaning they have Contracts with things like Time, Distance, Death, ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T01:58:09-07:00","id":101152,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think the Hedge might CAUSE Angels to fall. Given that the nature of the thorns is to slowly remove the traveler's soul, I would think that the Thorns, upon pricking the skin of the Angel's cover, would make said Angel divide by zero and Fall by being tainted by its nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T02:12:36-07:00","id":101157,"title":"","content":"I really like this idea! The reason TGM doesn't send folks in there is because it loses them... or rather it sends in cultists, changelings it has offered protection/considerations to and so on. Not angels, humans and human-ish things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T04:48:15-07:00","id":101192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=101068#post101068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you read my post at all? Your Demon form isn't supposed to be the method you use to regain Aether, its a small concession prize because it means you are already opening up to the God Machines Radar and that is dangerous virtually everywhere. But going someplace far removed from the Godmachine opens up the option, its one of the main principles of why Demons are trying to make Hell. You have produced no reason at all for why it should not work from what we know in the core rules, you are only guessing that it work because for some reason its an exception.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, come on now. Just because I disagree with you and your stance is no reason to suddenly get condescending. <br /> <br /> Making another world into a part of your own Hell is possible (its one of the many options put forward by the Tempters, but not what I'd call a &quot;main&quot; one), though it will require work, effort, and building your own source of aether somehow. Achieving Hell should not be so easy as just using Rip The Gates and settling in an abandoned part of the Astral, or Hisil, or whatever. Even Madam Damnation's little hell shard is built of transformed Infrastructure and constant vigilance against invading demons/angels. <br /> <br /> As for evidence? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 110</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Aether is as present as the God-Machine, its servants, and its manifestations (which is to say, terrifyingly common in some places and sparse to the point of nonexistence in others). That's part of the reason why, even though they don't require Aether to survive, demons rarely withdraw into hermitage somewhere the God Machine shows no presence - few would want to risk being discovered in a situatino where they have no ready way to recover their primary power source.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can just zip into demon form to regain aether in some remote, GM-less area, and regain a good amount of aether, that counts as a ready supply. Which is directly against what the very first lines of the Regaining Aether section talks about. There's talk about the demon form being a receptor and absorbing ambient aether, not generating them. There's talk about how aether is directly a bi product of the God Machine's efforts - it doesn't make sense to have aether equally floating around in an area where there's never been Gears as right next to a large city that's half Infrastructure. <br /> <br /> There's lots of reasons and evidence in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T05:03:19-07:00","id":101200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=101061#post101061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I can see Inquisitors going to the hedge for knowledge tempter their for pacts with gentry's. Psycho chomps for whatever resource they want and for most demons a place to hide I don't think the god machine has a lot of angels in the hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes and no. The God Machine Chronicle book leaves the question of Gears in Other Realms up to the ST. Which means the presence or lack of angels depends on the individual settings. There could be enough in the other realms so that its easy to have Hunter angels show. <br /> <br /> Just think - a hunter angel built to hunt in the Hedge could adopt a briarwolf cover, while one in the Hisil could be a Solar spirit, and a psychopomp in the Underworld! Lots of potential!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-29-2014, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:50:53-07:00","id":101299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=100967#post100967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of that whole thing, to be honest, the only one that is potentially problematic are Realms. Props, Actors and Swarms all have stats (and as such can be killed, as outlined by Satchel :P ). By the very virtue of the fact that they have stats, it controls how many titles a Fae can have (because a Title gives Fae stats).<br /> <br /> And let's be honest here, if you're capable of bringing the axe down on an Actor or Swarm, you've got the capability to defeat a Fae's story for a Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Luna likely has some ridiculously potent Bans. You know. Given what she is. That Predator Clause is just as applicable to her without stats, as it is a whole rather than piecemeal potent True Fae. Hell, one of their very Title powers is &quot;I can be destroyed as a prop in only one very particular way. That's it. Of course I'm limited on my interactions but...&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah. Because when you're a high ranking spirit, you totally don't have Bans. And people totally can't figure them out when you're dealing with other god tiers.<br /> <br /> Luna isn't that much different. Her &quot;Titles&quot; are effectively her Lunes. If she's remotely a thing of the Shadow, she has bans. It's fairly tit for tat to be honest, one doesn't by their very nature have a stark advantage over the other save in their respective realms. Your a celestial body riddled with spirit limitations. I'm my own reality who accepts limitations to create context and conflict (and seemingly not for much else). Lets fight. Or fuck. (Cue the next Wooing of Luna by the Duke of the Lunargent Thorn).<br /> <br /> Then again, that's a bit pointless too; why the hell go where something else has a home-turf advantage directly? You can enter a Fae's reality. You can enter Luna's chunk of the Shadow. You'll primarily be interacting with avatars/manifestations of them in the end, never the entity directly itself (even with the True Fae unless it was the weakest of their lot). You can fuck around, and they all have some limitation to overall &quot;I do what I want&quot;. Until you start hunting down their particular weaknesses at least. The Predator Clause is a bit misplaced in that regard; you can off her &quot;titles&quot;. You can guaranteed off her as well, but given the cosmic scope you wouldn't see it in a timeline that's game relevant beyond as an epic plot.<br /> <br /> But, you know... a Gentry -totally- wouldn't think to figure out her Bans as part of some epic quest to avoid being bored. Perish the thought! &quot;I was promised the moon would end and she'd never again sully the night. I'm making good on that.&quot; Cue epic guitar solo, the donning of cosmic shades and a rag-tag group of Gentry trapezing about the various realms in search of how. Fixing the Iron issue got boring anyhow (besides, there are already many potentials on how to be rid of it, snuffing out the moon prematurely? Now THAT is interesting.) Or, more likely, roping in some high potency PCs to do some dirty work on both's fronts (far more interesting).<br /> <br /> More seriously it's pretty pointless. At best we refer back to Imperial Mysteries which is -very- problematic outside of the Mage line, and at worst you get an Immovable Object meets an Unstoppable Force scenario going around in circles until one fan becomes blue in the face. They're little bitches in each others abodes. They all have some severe limitations on either direct interactions or inbuilt weaknesses (unless you magically start saying Luna doesn't follow the context she exists in regarding spirits, which is as much a cop-out as some of the prior anti-Gentry posits). They all can be exploited. But outside of some fun theorizing, it's pretty much the old CWOD &quot;My uber NPC can kick yours ass, because its my preferred gameline!&quot; trend that was common back in the day.<br /> <br /> They don't follow each others rules or systems, or any actual hard cap. That's Mage, and mage does not write the scoop for the other lines (and never has contrary to what some folks seem to try to reinforce to chagrin of everyone else). Seriously, Imperial Mysteries is about as irrelevant as you can get when it comes to the various game lines not Mage.<br /> <br /> How does Demon register into all this? Tough to say. I'm looking forwards to seeing more on the whole &quot;building Hell&quot; angle, but taken in of itself, it doesn't quite play all that well with the other gamelines either. Nor did I expect it to; they're designed to be the most fun within their own context, not be neutered by another unrelated gameline. So, making a giant cosmic levle melting pot and trying to shoehorn one setting/game's assumptions onto the other? Meh. Not sure what's being accomplished beyond stroking this or that Mage fanboy/fangirl's ego indirectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 03-29-2014, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T21:41:13-07:00","id":101744,"title":"","content":"It's been awhile since I've brushed up on my changeling mechanics but do True Fae, at least while in Arcadia, play by the 'so powerful they usually aren't represented by game stats' rule? I know that a lot of things have recently been given methods to be stated when dealing with other things that are powerful enough that how strong they are in comparison actually matters, but are the Gentry one of those things that are assumed to be stat-less outside of those situations? If so, I would assume that anything not thematically on the level of archmages and high level spirits are still subject to them being essentially stat-less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T05:05:04-07:00","id":101867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=101744#post101744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been awhile since I've brushed up on my changeling mechanics but do True Fae, at least while in Arcadia, play by the 'so powerful they usually aren't represented by game stats' rule? I know that a lot of things have recently been given methods to be stated when dealing with other things that are powerful enough that how strong they are in comparison actually matters, but are the Gentry one of those things that are assumed to be stat-less outside of those situations? If so, I would assume that anything not thematically on the level of archmages and high level spirits are still subject to them being essentially stat-less.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes and no. Rather, there's a tier 4 game that uses completely different rules from the standard, in their own style of game. And, yes, the Gentry are on the same level of archmages and high rank spirits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:07:04-07:00","id":101963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=101299#post101299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then again, that's a bit pointless too; why the hell go where something else has a home-turf advantage directly? You can enter a Fae's reality. You can enter Luna's chunk of the Shadow. You'll primarily be interacting with avatars/manifestations of them in the end, never the entity directly itself (even with the True Fae unless it was the weakest of their lot).<br /> <br /> But, you know... a Gentry -totally- wouldn't think to figure out her Bans as part of some epic quest to avoid being bored. Perish the thought! &quot;I was promised the moon would end and she'd never again sully the night. I'm making good on that.&quot; Cue epic guitar solo, the donning of cosmic shades and a rag-tag group of Gentry trapezing about the various realms in search of how. Fixing the Iron issue got boring anyhow (besides, there are already many potentials on how to be rid of it, snuffing out the moon prematurely? Now THAT is interesting.) Or, more likely, roping in some high potency PCs to do some dirty work on both's fronts (far more interesting).<br /> <br /> More seriously it's pretty pointless. At best we refer back to Imperial Mysteries which is -very- problematic outside of the Mage line, and at worst you get an Immovable Object meets an Unstoppable Force scenario going around in circles until one fan becomes blue in the face. They're little bitches in each others abodes. They all have some severe limitations on either direct interactions or inbuilt weaknesses (unless you magically start saying Luna doesn't follow the context she exists in regarding spirits, which is as much a cop-out as some of the prior anti-Gentry posits). They all can be exploited. But outside of some fun theorizing, it's pretty much the old CWOD &quot;My uber NPC can kick yours ass, because its my preferred gameline!&quot; trend that was common back in the day.<br /> <br /> They don't follow each others rules or systems, or any actual hard cap. That's Mage, and mage does not write the scoop for the other lines (and never has contrary to what some folks seem to try to reinforce to chagrin of everyone else). Seriously, Imperial Mysteries is about as irrelevant as you can get when it comes to the various game lines not Mage.<br /> <br /> How does Demon register into all this? Tough to say. I'm looking forwards to seeing more on the whole &quot;building Hell&quot; angle, but taken in of itself, it doesn't quite play all that well with the other gamelines either. Nor did I expect it to; they're designed to be the most fun within their own context, not be neutered by another unrelated gameline. So, making a giant cosmic levle melting pot and trying to shoehorn one setting/game's assumptions onto the other? Meh. Not sure what's being accomplished beyond stroking this or that Mage fanboy/fangirl's ego indirectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a thread that is about Demon interacting with either True Fae for Arcadia I find the amount of True Fae vs Luna discussion sorta weird in this thread. However I felt Tatterdemalion King did bring up some good points.<br /> <br /> As Tatterdemalion King points out Luna/High Rank Spirits and True Fae are kinda (if you squint and look side on) similar beings. Also my earlier comment about the &quot;love&quot; True Fae receive is pretty well summed up with ideas like:<br /> True Fae romancing Luna (because the Fae and Spirit worlds really interact so often in the Werewolf/Changeling books/fluff/mechanics).<br /> Giving up on fixing the Iron problem because ways they already half figured out to do it (because god forbid a hard and fast aspect of reality they can't fuck around with exists).<br /> The True Fae can travel to any realm attached to our reality (last I checked they were limited to the material world, Hedge, Arcadia and the Dream sub-realm of the Astral).<br /> <br /> Of course, all this stuff is completely subjective to ones and the ST can do what they want within their game. Likewise, I get that a lot of what Tatterdemalion King said was in jest, fun and with a bit of sarcasm. I'm pointing out some of the example he gave because they are the sort of thing I've run into before unironically that people have stated about True Fae.<br /> <br /> I agree that Imperial Mysteries is problematic. However, I think its only problematic when people try and apply its metaphysics/idea outside of the Mage cosmology/game line. I used to be one of those &quot;Mage fanboys&quot; that Tatterdemalion King mentioned. However, I kinda got fed up with increasingly worse explanations that Mage tried to supply about the other game lines and basically wrote Mages off as not really knowning much more then any other supernatural in the NWoD. Despite my separation from the Mage line for a while I feel it would be remiss of me to not point out that I've noticed the number of &quot;Changeling Fanboys&quot; is at least equal to the Mage ones. Though they are less obtrusive about their preference by about a hairs breadth.<br /> <br /> Interestingly I always got the impression in CWoD that certain metaphysically empowered beings were more powerful then others. That while the argument between fan's could occur, the writers would pretty much decide the relative powers and abilities and determine the victor as need be for that settings metaplot. For example, the Gehenna book pretty much outright states that Tzimisce is more powerful then Giovanni or Tremere because they are younger antediluvian. Likewise Lilith is more powerful then Caine according to least one Gehenna scenario. As for cross-line interactions in CWoD see the Week of Nightmares stuff. Ravnos stomps a lot of stuff including some very, very powerful characters from other game lines. In the end the Mages kill him using smarts and technomagic.<br /> <br /> It might just be my taste, but I'm fine with that. The idea that all supernaturals have an &quot;equal&quot; slice of the metaphysical pie when it comes to the validity of their arguments about the nature of reality, the reason they exist and all have equal &quot;end games&quot;/metaphysical beings looking over them is a very NWoD idea.<br /> <br /> Before I seem to accusatory of any particular view point (I find the Changeling fanboyism towards True Fae annoying but that's about it) I want to say I agree with the general consensus that any of the &quot;god-tier&quot; supernaturals in the NWoD win in their own realm if they get in a fight there. For me this includes the God Machine (or at least its archangels) in the material universe. I'd also say their could be exceptions to said rules, if your using Mage and want Archmasters to go around being the wild cards that shake up the worlds metaphysics then let them beable to storm other realms to do stuff. That's an ST choice though, same as saying the True Fae can realm hope to have adventures for the sake of not being board. Its oranges and apples at that point.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the answer to this thread <b>has been summed up a half dozen times</b> already:<br /> <br /> 1)Demons can beat True Fae in the real world if they've for the stats for it or use their powers cleverly.<br /> <br /> 2)Demons can't really &quot;beat&quot; a True Fae in Arcadia but might be able to pull some sort of fast one to at least not get insta-screwed or escape. Maybe...that's up the ST at the end of the day.<br /> <br /> 3)Demons can oppose True Fae in the Hedge, but likely want to be baseline a bit more powerful (Primum 6+) if they do so.<br /> <br /> One final point I'd like to raise as a final point to my position on the True Fae issue. I find the True Fae &quot;messy&quot; as metaphysical beings go. They are not defined by anything save their agreements with things/concepts/etc and this should give them a fixed nature to a certain extent. It does not, they flang all over the metaphysical rules that all other creatures of equivalent power in the other game lines have to obey without question.<br /> <br /> Honestly its one of the reason (along with the Mage issues I've already discussed) why I moved away from a completely inclusive model of the NWoD. These days I have each game happen in its own world, with maybe minor crossover occuring (say 2 maybe 3 game lines e.g. Vampire, Demon, Promethean).<br /> <br /> Its also why I think I prefer the Demon and Mage (the earlier bits that make sense) fluff in general, it all structured and ordered because that part of the points of the game. In one a giant machine is running the universe. In the other a bunch of evil mega-mages made the universe this way to trap everyone in it and keep their monopoly on godhood. It all structured and ordered and works on rules and ideas that can at least be passed off for a sort of solid metaphysical theory akin to the ones that you might see in a philosophy textbook or high level physics (one again looking sideways and squinting).<br /> <br /> I guess I find Changelings idea that everything runs off of story's and tropes and deals and contracts and &quot;what fate says&quot; is all a little &quot;soft&quot; and odd for me. It's not no absolutes, it all messy and changes on a case by case basis and such. That's not to my taste, it does not make it bad, but its not to my taste and I guess its really, really annoying in cases where people then drag that messy indistinct narrative based metaphysics into other games that have set mechanical metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Its like a Demon player bringing a maths textbook and says:<br /> <br /> &quot;This is Maths, it provides the basis for human understanding and its principles have been infinitely useful to mankind.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Changeling player brings an art textbook and says:<br /> <br /> &quot;This is Art, it enriches our lives and gives us a different perspective on how we see thing. It's helped us grow as a species.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Demon player then tries to explain why maths is obviously more important and how useful it is. He shows why maths is important, tires to point out the number of things that require maths at their foundation to even work.<br /> <br /> The Changeling player then tries to explain why Art is so important, He tries to explain what Art has contributed to human development in general and civilization in particular.<br /> <br /> The point is neither is going to win their argument. They are basically using different languages and the things that they are point out as so important as points why their thing is so good carry very little relevance or merit within the other thing/subjects worldview or field of practice. Its literally science vs art.<br /> <br /> I may have other thought this issue a bit...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:44:31-07:00","id":103763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=101963#post101963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double