nyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T06:11:34-07:00","id":103991,"title":"","content":"Early prototype angels that didn't so much fall as all decide to take an indefinite vacation until their working conditions were improved?<br /> And for a vacation, of course, you need somewhere to go that ISN'T your workplace, and since the entire world is the workplace of TGM... well, just get to it, building a vacation paradise world! (aka hell)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T06:57:13-07:00","id":104010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=103899#post103899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> remember that story that the Faeries are angels too good for Hell yet too wicked for Heaven? And remember that that story was one of the options in Changeling? If that's so- than what the hell IS the Hedge?...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in real life Faeries are considered neutral angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T08:16:02-07:00","id":104057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=103958#post103958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Officially, the Hedge is the border between Faerie and Reality - its like the Gauntlet, but much wider. Its FAERIE you should be wondering about!</div> </div> </div> </div>what I meant was that if we use the folktale in which Faeries are &quot;neutral Angels&quot;, which has fallen because of the Hedge (and that in turn made them into the Gentry instead of Exiles), than the Hedge was before Faerie- and in that case, what is the Hedge if it is strong enough to corrupt Angels?<br /> <br /> (again, this is crossover territory and the GM plays a role in it, so it may not be everyone's &quot;cup of tea&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T08:34:08-07:00","id":104065,"title":"","content":"Angels have to fall because of their own free will choice. In the legend of fae = &quot;neutral angel,&quot; the fae were born because they choose not to take a side in the war between angels and demons. And were outcast because of that choice, but not hunted.<br /> <br /> I see the Hedge as more an expression of those &quot;neutral-angels&quot; than the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T10:45:38-07:00","id":104152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=103899#post103899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> remember that story that the Faeries are angels too good for Hell yet too wicked for Heaven? And remember that that story was one of the options in Changeling? If that's so- than what the hell IS the Hedge?...</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I fancy the idea that the Hedge is an overgrown, untrimmed garden.<br /> Like the Garden of Eden, but gone horribly wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T11:41:44-07:00","id":104211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=104152#post104152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I fancy the idea that the Hedge is an overgrown, untrimmed garden.<br /> Like the Garden of Eden, but gone horribly wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to apply that metaphor to the spirit wilds and peg the Hedge as the metaphorical overlap between the wilds, the Autochthonous Depths, and any other zone of the cosmology that can be described as &quot;border zone between Earth and the home(s) of (a) god(s).&quot;<br /> <br /> I note with some interest that, if one doesn't mind treating with crossover, Faerie could be pointed to as potentially a successful Tempter-Hell \u2014 nobody gets in without an invitation, it's bordered by a region that skews toward the symbolism of places where the Machine doesn't have a great deal of presence, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T10:44:10-07:00","id":104938,"title":"","content":"I had a more interesting thought after reading about Demon deals. What if instead of highly successful demons, the Fae are the original creatures that the God machine turns into Angels? This would explain a few things: Why the god machine is not actively at war with the Fae (he needs them, they're raw materials) why Angels are so hard to create (harvesting a fricken true Fae?!?) and why, when they fall, Demons suddenly manifest the ability to make deals - it's what's left of the fae spirit coming through.<br /> <br /> So basically, Fae aren't successful demons, Demons are just what happens when you tame a fae and make its domain the mortal realm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T14:21:54-07:00","id":105083,"title":"","content":"Consider this idea. You know how Fae abide by rules and all, even defining their bodies? Each Fae is an alien and limitless being, until it agrees to rules. Once it interacts with these rules, Fae can interact with each other and the earth. By agreeing to be partly real, each fae takes titles, agrees to rules (like the no god mode rule, the rules of widdershins titles, the rule of 6-dot trait limits in the mortal world, etc). Only by running their wyld-essence through this fate-spinning mechanism allows them, via game traits and mechanical rules, to interact. And who/what are these rules, or who made/maintains them? The Machine, of course. Only by agreeing to ITs laws are the Fae able to interact with WoD shards. Only by taking upon the same laws God enforces on everyone allows Fae to Manifest, to play the Game of Immortals, etc. Because without the Machine, there are no rules, no mechanics, no traits.. just raw Arcadian chaos. That is why the Fae do not destroy the Machine, even if they could.. they are too fascinated by it, too addicted to the games they can play when Reality is enforced and Rules occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T14:32:22-07:00","id":105096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/100060-demons-and-true-fae-or-arcadia-in-general?p=104010#post104010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well in real life Faeries are considered neutral angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on who you ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}